From 7354ae32310317808a74e94b3d0e13aa9c113644 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 08:14:52 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 083/145] media: meson: vdec: hevc: resync at the next IRAP
 after a stall recovery

codec_hevc_stall_recover() drops the in-flight frame to get the firmware
running again, but leaves the decoder decoding. That frame is a reference
for everything up to the next keyframe, so every following frame fails its
reference lookup:

  meson-vdec: decode stall (status=00000004 lcu=400003db) - recovering in place
  meson-vdec: Couldn't find ref. frame 63     (x32)

Each of those takes a substitute frame and is reconstructed from the wrong
pixels. The result is seconds of visible corruption in exchange for one
dropped frame, which is worse than showing nothing: a decoder that cannot
reconstruct a picture correctly should not display it.

The driver already has the right mechanism. codec_hevc_process_segment()
skips slices while hevc->seen_irap is clear, which is how a session fed
from the middle of a GOP waits for its first keyframe. seen_irap is set
once at stream start and never cleared, so recovery cannot reuse it.

Clear it during recovery. The decoder then idles until the next IRAP and
resumes cleanly, and no substituted reference is ever programmed into the
MC engine - which also keeps the recovery path away from the canvas-slot
hazard that the substitution in codec_hevc_set_ref_list() exists to
contain.

Observed on a 4K HDR 59.94fps stream carrying one genuinely illegal frame
(cu_qp_delta -34, outside the H.265 range [-32,31]); the firmware wedges at
status 0x4 with the LCU counter frozen, reproducibly at the same position.

Signed-off-by: Gus Bourg <gus@bourg.net>
---
 drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
index 597cef06454c..5dff79217302 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_hevc.c
@@ -1514,6 +1514,25 @@ static void codec_hevc_stall_recover(struct amvdec_session *sess)
 	amvdec_write_dos(core, HEVC_STREAM_CONTROL, s_ctrl);
 	amvdec_write_dos(core, HEVC_SHIFT_BYTE_COUNT, s_shift);
 
+	/*
+	 * Resynchronise at the next IRAP rather than resuming mid-GOP.
+	 *
+	 * The frame dropped below is a reference for everything that
+	 * follows it until the next keyframe.  Carrying on decodes those
+	 * frames against a reference that no longer exists: each one fails
+	 * its lookup ("Couldn't find ref. frame N"), takes a substitute,
+	 * and is reconstructed from the wrong pixels - seconds of visible
+	 * corruption for one bad frame, which is worse than showing
+	 * nothing.
+	 *
+	 * codec_hevc_process_segment() already skips slices while
+	 * seen_irap is clear, which is how a session that starts mid-GOP
+	 * finds its feet.  Clearing it here reuses exactly that path: the
+	 * decoder idles until the next IRAP and then resumes cleanly, with
+	 * no substituted references programmed into the MC engine at all.
+	 */
+	hevc->seen_irap = 0;
+
 	/* Drop the poisoned in-flight frame, recycle its buffer */
 	if (hevc->cur_frame) {
 		struct hevc_frame *f = hevc->cur_frame;
-- 
